Z||000000||drednot||09-16-2001||01:32 PM||||Here is the deal, One of my neighbors has a 1981 DeLorean that has 160,000 miles on it.  The engine (PRV-6) is fried.  It was his driver up until 2 years ago.  The stainless steel body is in fair shape with only a few dings on it, and warped front facia.  I think I can get this car cheep, like under $1000.  My question- Can I use a PRV-6 from a Eagle Premier?  I know of one with under 60,000 miles on that I can get.  Now, I know it is the same engine, but is it interchangeable?  Any help is welcome.||||reg||11
